+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deploy review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.**
+
+The contract as it stands **cannot take a single deposit on mainnet** — `deposit()` reverts
+unconditionally against the real USDT at `0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7`. If that one
+line were fixed, the vault would then be a yield vault that pays no yield: 100% of the Aave interest,
+plus every withdrawal fee, is permanently unreachable by anyone including the owner. On top of that,
+the owner can drain an incoming deposit with a single unprivileged-looking parameter change.
+
+The 39 green tests are green because the test doubles are the wrong shape. `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol`
+is a stock OpenZeppelin ERC20 that returns `bool` — real USDT does not. `test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol`
+mints aTokens 1:1 and never accrues interest — real Aave does. The suite therefore never exercises
+the two things the vault actually depends on. `forge coverage` reports 100% of lines and functions
+on `src/UsdtYieldVault.sol` and is not wrong; line coverage measures which lines ran, not whether
+what they did was correct.
+
+Nothing under `src/`, `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol`, or `test/mocks/` was modified. All new work is in
+`test/audit/`.
+
+---
+
