+# C-2 — Aave yield is never credited to anyone and is permanently unrecoverable
+
+**Severity: Critical (the vault does not do the one thing it is named after).**
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:97`, `:117`, `:144` — `totalAssetsStored` is a mirror the contract writes to
+on deposit and withdraw. It is never reconciled against `aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this))`.
+
+Aave pays interest by growing the aToken balance. The vault's `totalAssets()` returns the mirror, so
+share price is pinned to `deposits / shares` forever. Depositors receive back principal minus fees,
+never a unit of interest. The interest accumulates in the vault's Aave position, and **there is no
+function anywhere in the contract that can move it** — `withdraw` is the only exit and it can only
+ever pay out `convertToAssets(shares)`, which is computed from the same frozen mirror. No sweep, no
+rescue, no `harvest`. Once the last share is burned, `totalShares == 0` and `totalAssetsStored == 0`
+while the aToken balance is still positive; a new depositor resets the accounting and cannot reach it
+either.
+
+At the real USDT supply rate on the pinned block, that is **360.16 USDT lost on a single 10,000 USDT
+deposit held for one year** — see the `test_RealAaveYieldIsInvisibleToTheVaultAndUnrecoverable` log
+in the C-1 evidence above (`real aUSDT after 1y: 10330.163105`, `vault.totalAssets(): 10000.000000`,
+`stranded in aave forever: 360.163105`; the extra 30 USDT over the interest is the withdrawal fee,
+see H-1).
+
+### Evidence
+
+Property, red:
+
+```
+[FAIL: sole depositor must own the 10% yield: 1000000000 !~= 1100000000 (max delta: 1, real delta: 100000000)] test_Property_DepositorEarnsAaveYield() (gas: 255586)
+[FAIL: accounting must match reality: 1000000000 != 1050000000] test_Property_TotalAssetsTracksTheAavePosition() (gas: 256816)
+[FAIL: nothing may be stranded after a full exit: 103000000 != 0] test_Property_VaultCanBeFullyDrained() (gas: 273079)
+```
+
+Quantified, and fuzzed across deposit sizes and yield rates:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/audit/VaultAccounting.t.sol' -vv
+Ran 11 tests for test/audit/VaultAccountingTest
+[PASS] testFuzz_VaultNeverCreditsInterest(uint96,uint16) (runs: 256, μ: 218011, ~: 217864)
+[PASS] test_AaveYieldIsUnrecoverableByEveryone() (gas: 224808)
+Logs:
+  stranded aUSDT (6dp): 103.000000
+```
+
+(1,000 USDT deposited, Aave pays 10%, sole depositor withdraws everything, receives 997 USDT,
+103 USDT left behind with zero shares outstanding.)
+
+Stateful invariant, red after two calls (a deposit and an interest accrual):
+
+```
+$ rm -rf cache/invariant && forge test --match-path 'test/audit/VaultInvariants.t.sol'
+Ran 3 tests for test/audit/VaultInvariants.t.sol:VaultInvariantsTest
+[FAIL: unaccounted USDT stuck in aave: 138341777634 != 136512510000]
+	[Sequence] (original: 3, shrunk: 2)
+		sender=0x00000000000000000000000000000000000F4240 addr=[test/audit/VaultInvariants.t.sol:VaultHandler]0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9 calldata=deposit(uint256,uint256) args=[51595818 [5.159e7], 1039529418387339277703581644429675260301187071882390 [1.039e51]]
+		sender=0x52D70E2FF31a197D491Fa75eCcA36d1d42054EcD addr=[test/audit/VaultInvariants.t.sol:VaultHandler]0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9 calldata=accrue(uint256) args=[335]
+ invariant_NoUnaccountedFunds() (runs: 0, calls: 0, reverts: 0)
+[PASS] invariant_SharesAccountingIsConsistent() (runs: 256, calls: 128000, reverts: 0)
+[PASS] invariant_VaultIsNeverMateriallyInsolvent() (runs: 256, calls: 128000, reverts: 0)
+Suite result: FAILED. 2 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 14.64s
+```
+
+### Fix
+
+Delete `totalAssetsStored` and derive `totalAssets()` from the position itself:
+
+```solidity
+function totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {
+    return aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this));
+}
+```
+
+aUSDT is rebasing, so its `balanceOf` already is the principal-plus-interest figure, and
+`convertToShares` / `convertToAssets` then price shares correctly with no reconciliation step and no
+drift. Note the standard consequence: reading a live balance reintroduces the ERC4626 first-depositor
+inflation/donation attack that the mirror accidentally prevented, so pair this with virtual
+shares/assets (OZ ERC4626 `_decimalsOffset`) or a dead-shares mint on first deposit. Removing the
+mirror also fixes H-1 and the 1-unit rounding tolerance noted under `invariant_VaultIsNeverMaterially-
+Insolvent`. Strongly consider inheriting OZ's `ERC4626` rather than hand-rolling share maths.
