+# H-1 — The withdrawal fee is destroyed, not redistributed; the docs say otherwise
+
+**Severity: High (silent, permanent value loss on every exit).**
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:117-119`:
+
+```solidity
+totalAssetsStored -= grossAssets;      // removes gross
+aavePool.withdraw(address(usdt), netAssets, msg.sender);   // withdraws net
+```
+
+The contract's own NatSpec (`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:17-18`) states: *"Both fees stay supplied in Aave
+and accrue to the remaining shareholders rather than being swept to the owner."* That is true of the
+deposit fee and false of the withdrawal fee. Because the mirror is decremented by `grossAssets` while
+only `netAssets` leaves Aave, the fee is subtracted from the accounting *and* left in the pool. Share
+price for the remaining holders is unchanged, so nobody receives it. It joins the C-2 pile of
+unreachable funds.
+
+Unlike C-2 this bites even if Aave paid 0% — it is 0.3% of every withdrawal, forever.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+[FAIL: the fee must land on bob's shares: 1000000000 != 1003000000] test_Property_WithdrawFeeAccruesToRemainingShareholders() (gas: 345809)
+```
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/audit/VaultAccounting.t.sol' -vv
+[PASS] test_WithdrawFeeIsStrandedNotDistributedToRemainingHolders() (gas: 278915)
+[PASS] test_UnaccountedGapGrowsWithEveryWithdrawal() (gas: 345014)
+Logs:
+  unreachable USDT after 5 partial exits (6dp): 29.062500
+```
+
+Two depositors at 1,000 USDT each; one exits; the remaining holder's redeemable balance is
+1,000.000000 before and 1,000.000000 after, while the vault's Aave position is 1,003.000000 against a
+`totalAssets()` of 1,000.000000. Five partial exits from a 20,000 USDT vault leave 29.06 USDT
+unreachable, and the gap is asserted to grow monotonically.
+
+### Fix
+
+If the fee is meant to stay with the remaining shareholders, decrement by the net amount:
+`totalAssetsStored -= netAssets;`. If `totalAssets()` is switched to read `aUsdt.balanceOf(...)` per
+C-2, this bug disappears on its own — the fee stays in the position and the price per share rises for
+whoever is left. If instead the fee is meant to be protocol revenue, add an explicit
+`feeRecipient` and transfer it. Either way, pick one and make the NatSpec match. Add an assertion in
+CI that a withdrawal leaves `totalAssets()` and the aToken balance equal.
+
