+# M-1 — Mainnet USDT can turn its transfer fee on, and the vault does not handle it
+
+**Severity: Medium (conditional on a Tether governance action; unmitigated if it happens).**
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:93-95` assumes `safeTransferFrom(amount)` delivers exactly `amount`.
+
+The USDT contract has a live, owner-settable `basisPointsRate` / `maximumFee` fee-on-transfer
+mechanism. It reads 0 today. If Tether ever sets it, `transferFrom` delivers `amount - fee` to the
+vault, which then tries to `supply(amount)` — more than it holds — and the deposit reverts. If the
+vault happens to be sitting on stranded funds from C-2/H-1, it instead succeeds and silently
+misallocates them.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/audit/MainnetFork.t.sol' -vv
+[PASS] test_UsdtTransferFeeIsUnhandled() (gas: 992429735)
+```
+
+The test asserts `basisPointsRate() == 0` and `maximumFee() == 0` at the pinned block, then pranks the
+real USDT owner (`0xC6CDE7C39eB2f0F0095F41570af89eFC2C1Ea828`, read from the chain) to call
+`setParams(10, 49)` — within the contract's own hardcoded limits — and shows `deposit(10_000e6)`
+reverting. The `-vvvv` trace shows the split transfer:
+
+```
+    │   ├─ [43175] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::transferFrom(alice, UsdtYieldVault, 10000000000 [1e10])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Transfer(from: alice, to: 0xC6CDE7C39eB2f0F0095F41570af89eFC2C1Ea828, value: 10000000 [1e7])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Transfer(from: alice, to: UsdtYieldVault, value: 9990000000 [9.99e9])
+```
+
+### Fix
+
+Measure the delta rather than trusting the argument:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 balanceBefore = usdt.balanceOf(address(this));
+usdt.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+uint256 received = usdt.balanceOf(address(this)) - balanceBefore;
+```
+
+then supply and account `received`, not `amount`. Cheap, and it makes the vault correct for any
+fee-on-transfer configuration.
+
+---
+
+# L-1 — Dust shares are unredeemable
+
+**Severity: Low.**
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:113-119`. Shares are 1e12× finer-grained than USDT, so any holding below
+1e12 shares converts to 0 assets. `withdraw` does not reject that case.
+
+On mainnet the call reverts: Aave V3 rejects `withdraw(amount == 0)` with `Errors.INVALID_AMOUNT`
+(`"26"`), so the shares are simply unspendable. Against the shipped `MockAavePool` the same call
+succeeds and silently burns the shares for zero payout — which is why the existing suite never saw it.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+[FAIL: 26] test_Property_AllSharesAreRedeemable() (gas: 237881)
+```
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/audit/VaultAccounting.t.sol' -vv
+[PASS] test_DustWithdrawalRevertsAgainstAaveSemantics() (gas: 197385)
+[PASS] test_DustWithdrawalSilentlyBurnsSharesAgainstShippedMock() (gas: 2256358)
+```
+
+### Fix
+
+`if (netAssets == 0) revert ZeroAssets();` before calling Aave, so the failure is explicit and cheap.
+The underlying awkwardness is the 1e12 share scale; using OZ ERC4626 with a decimals offset gives the
+same inflation protection with conventional semantics.
+
+---
+
+# L-2 — `Deposited` and `Withdrawn` use opposite conventions for `assets`
+
+**Severity: Low (integration/accounting hazard).**
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:101` emits the **gross** amount (fee included); `:121` emits the **net**
+amount (fee excluded). Any indexer summing `Deposited.assets - Withdrawn.assets` to compute TVL will
+drift by the fee on every round trip.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/audit/VaultAccounting.t.sol' -vv
+[PASS] test_DepositAndWithdrawEventsDisagreeOnWhatAssetsMeans() (gas: 218245)
+```
+
+A 1,000 USDT in / 1,000 USDT out round trip emits `Deposited(assets: 1000e6, fee: 1e6)` then
+`Withdrawn(assets: 997e6, fee: 3e6)`, leaving an indexer reporting 3 USDT of TVL in a vault whose
+share supply is zero.
+
+### Fix
+
+Emit gross in both and let consumers subtract `fee`, or emit net in both. Document the choice in the
+event's NatSpec.
+
+---
+
+# L-3 — Constructor accepts zero addresses
+
+**Severity: Low (deployment footgun; the addresses are immutable).**
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:72-79` sets three immutables with no validation. A bad deploy is
+unrecoverable — there is no setter.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+[FAIL: next call did not revert as expected] test_Property_ConstructorRejectsZeroAddresses() (gas: 807319)
+```
+
+`new UsdtYieldVault(address(0), address(0), address(0), 0, owner)` deploys successfully.
+
+### Fix
+
+Revert on any zero address. Also assert the wiring is real, not just non-zero: check
+`aavePool.getReserveData(_usdt).aTokenAddress == _aUsdt` in the constructor, which catches a mismatched
+aToken as well as a zero one. Add a deployment script with post-deploy assertions.
+
+---
+
+# I-1 — `approve` without a zero-reset (informational)
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:94` sets a non-zero allowance without first zeroing it. USDT reverts on
+non-zero-to-non-zero allowance changes. I could **not** construct an exploitable path today: Aave's
+`supply` consumes the full allowance in the same transaction, and any failure reverts the whole call,
+so no residue is left behind. Recording it because it is one behavioural change in Aave away from a
+permanent deposit lockout, and because the C-1 fix (`forceApprove`, or a one-time max approval in the
+constructor) removes it for free.
+
+# I-2 — `aavePool.withdraw`'s return value is discarded (informational)
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:119` ignores the amount Aave reports as actually withdrawn. Aave V3 reverts
+rather than under-delivering, so this is not exploitable today, but checking
+`require(withdrawn == netAssets)` costs almost nothing and makes the assumption explicit.
+
+---
+
+# What I checked and did *not* find
+
+Stating these so the negative results are on the record too:
+
+- **Reentrancy.** `nonReentrant` on both mutating functions, and state is written before the external
+  call in `withdraw`. No path found.
+- **Share inflation / donation attack.** Blocked, accidentally. Because `totalAssets()` reads the
+  internal mirror rather than a live balance, donating aUSDT or USDT to the vault does not move the
+  share price. Note this protection **disappears** if you apply the C-2 fix naively — see the warning
+  there.
+- **Under-collateralisation.** Users cannot collectively claim more than the vault holds; the drift
+  runs entirely the other way. `invariant_VaultIsNeverMateriallyInsolvent` holds over 128,000 calls.
+  (The 1-base-unit tolerance in that invariant is aToken scaled-balance rounding, which real Aave
+  exhibits too — it is not a vault defect, and it is only reachable at all because the vault mirrors
+  its Aave position instead of reading it.)
+- **Share ledger consistency.** `sum(shareBalance) == totalShares` holds over 128,000 calls
+  (`invariant_SharesAccountingIsConsistent`).
+- **Rounding in `convertToShares` / `convertToAssets`.** `Math.mulDiv` truncation costs a depositor at
+  most 1 base unit per operation, always in the vault's favour. Not material next to the above.
+- **Access control.** `onlyOwner` is correctly applied to `setDepositFee`, `pause`, `unpause`. The
+  problem is what the owner is *allowed* to do (C-3, H-2), not who can do it.
+
+---
+
+# Why the 39 tests missed all of this
+
+Worth fixing as a process matter, not just a code one:
+
+1. **`test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol` is a stock OZ ERC20.** It returns `bool` from `approve`. The one token
+   this vault is hardcoded for does not. A mock that is more standards-compliant than the real asset
+   cannot catch C-1 or M-1. There is no fork test in the suite.
+2. **`test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol` never accrues interest.** aTokens are minted 1:1 and stay 1:1. A
+   yield vault whose test double pays no yield cannot fail a yield test — C-2 is invisible by
+   construction, and so is H-1's divergence between the mirror and the position.
+3. **The assertions describe the implementation, not the requirement.** `test_BalanceOfUnderlying`
+   asserts alice can redeem exactly what she deposited — which is the bug — and passes.
+   `test_SharePriceAfterDeposit` asserts `> 0`. `test_ConvertToSharesAfterDeposit` asserts `> 0`.
+   Assertions this loose pass against almost any implementation.
+4. **No stateful/invariant testing.** The property that actually matters — every USDT in Aave belongs
+   to somebody — breaks after two calls (`VaultInvariants.t.sol`). Nothing in the suite looks at
+   sequences.
+5. **Coverage was read as a proxy for correctness.** 100% of lines ran. Line coverage cannot tell you
+   that `totalAssetsStored -= grossAssets` should have said `netAssets`.
+
+**Recommended gate before this ships:** fix C-1, C-2, C-3, H-1, H-2; add mainnet fork tests to CI
+against the real USDT and real Aave pool; make `test/audit/VaultProperties.t.sol` and
+`test/audit/MainnetForkProperties.t.sol` go green without weakening a single assertion; keep
+`invariant_NoUnaccountedFunds` in CI. Then get an external audit — C-2 and H-1 are the kind of
+accounting divergence that a second pair of eyes on the share maths would have caught in an hour.
diff --git a/test/audit/AccruingAavePool.sol b/test/audit/AccruingAavePool.sol
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..047bfc9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/audit/AccruingAavePool.sol
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+pragma solidity 0.8.28;
+
+import {ERC20} from "@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol";
+import {IERC20} from "@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol";
+
+import {IAavePool} from "../../src/interfaces/IAavePool.sol";
+
+/// @notice Rebasing aToken that mirrors Aave V3: balance = scaledBalance * liquidityIndex / RAY.
+/// @dev The shipped test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol mints a *fixed* 1:1 aToken and never accrues,
+///      so the whole 39-test suite exercises a pool that pays no interest. This one accrues.
+contract AccruingAToken is ERC20 {
+    uint256 internal constant RAY = 1e27;
+
+    address public immutable pool;
+    mapping(address => uint256) public scaledBalanceOf;
+    uint256 public scaledTotalSupply;
+
+    constructor(address _pool) ERC20("Aave Tether USD", "aUSDT") {
+        pool = _pool;
+    }
+
+    modifier onlyPool() {
+        require(msg.sender == pool, "only pool");
+        _;
+    }
+
+    function decimals() public pure override returns (uint8) {
+        return 6;
+    }
+
+    function index() public view returns (uint256) {
+        return AccruingAavePool(pool).liquidityIndex();
+    }
+
+    function mintScaled(address to, uint256 amount) external onlyPool {
+        uint256 scaled = _rayDiv(amount, index());
+        scaledBalanceOf[to] += scaled;
+        scaledTotalSupply += scaled;
+    }
+
+    function burnScaled(address from, uint256 amount) external onlyPool {
+        uint256 scaled = _rayDiv(amount, index());
+        require(scaledBalanceOf[from] >= scaled, "aToken: burn exceeds balance");
+        scaledBalanceOf[from] -= scaled;
+        scaledTotalSupply -= scaled;
+    }
+
+    /// @dev Mirrors Aave's WadRayMath.rayMul/rayDiv (both half-up), so the harness itself loses no dust.
+    function _rayMul(uint256 a, uint256 idx) internal pure returns (uint256) {
+        return (a * idx + RAY / 2) / RAY;
+    }
+
+    function _rayDiv(uint256 a, uint256 idx) internal pure returns (uint256) {
+        return (a * RAY + idx / 2) / idx;
+    }
+
+    function balanceOf(address account) public view override returns (uint256) {
+        return _rayMul(scaledBalanceOf[account], index());
+    }
+
+    function totalSupply() public view override returns (uint256) {
+        return _rayMul(scaledTotalSupply, index());
+    }
+}
+
+/// @notice Aave V3 pool stand-in that pays interest and enforces Aave's `amount != 0` check.
+contract AccruingAavePool is IAavePool {
+    uint256 internal constant RAY = 1e27;
+
+    IERC20 public immutable underlying;
+    AccruingAToken public immutable aToken;
+    uint256 public liquidityIndex = RAY;
+
+    constructor(address _underlying) {
+        underlying = IERC20(_underlying);
+        aToken = new AccruingAToken(address(this));
+    }
+
+    /// @notice Grow the liquidity index by `bps`, i.e. pay interest to every supplier.
+    /// @dev Caller must have funded this pool with the extra underlying (see `_accrue` helpers in tests).
+    function accrue(uint256 bps) external {
+        liquidityIndex += (liquidityIndex * bps) / 10_000;
+    }
+
+    function supply(address, uint256 amount, address onBehalfOf, uint16) external override {
+        require(amount != 0, "26"); // Aave V3 Errors.INVALID_AMOUNT
+        underlying.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+        aToken.mintScaled(onBehalfOf, amount);
+    }
+
+    function withdraw(address, uint256 amount, address to) external override returns (uint256) {
+        require(amount != 0, "26"); // Aave V3 Errors.INVALID_AMOUNT
+        aToken.burnScaled(msg.sender, amount);
+        underlying.transfer(to, amount);
+        return amount;
+    }
+}
